A/B: env-backed u-boot bootcount on R3-mini (mt7986), foundation for A/B rollback.

Ported from bpi-r3 z02. Adds BOOTCOUNT_LIMIT/ENV/ALTBOOTCMD to R3-mini's two
media defconfigs (emmc/snand), after the AUTOBOOT_STOP_STR line z01 adds. The
counter is gated by the `upgrade_available` env var, so steady-state boots
neither count nor write flash; once it exceeds `bootlimit`, autoboot runs
altbootcmd (slot switch).

--- a/configs/mt7986a_bpi-r3-mini-emmc_defconfig
+++ b/configs/mt7986a_bpi-r3-mini-emmc_defconfig
@@ -22,6 +22,9 @@
 CONFIG_BOOTDELAY=1
 CONFIG_AUTOBOOT_KEYED=y
 CONFIG_AUTOBOOT_STOP_STR=" "
+CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_LIMIT=y
+CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_ENV=y
+CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_ALTBOOTCMD=y
 CONFIG_OF_SYSTEM_SETUP=y
 CONFIG_DEFAULT_FDT_FILE="mediatek/mt7986a-bpi-r3-mini.dtb"
 CONFIG_LOGLEVEL=7
--- a/configs/mt7986a_bpi-r3-mini-snand_defconfig
+++ b/configs/mt7986a_bpi-r3-mini-snand_defconfig
@@ -19,6 +19,9 @@
 CONFIG_BOOTDELAY=1
 CONFIG_AUTOBOOT_KEYED=y
 CONFIG_AUTOBOOT_STOP_STR=" "
+CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_LIMIT=y
+CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_ENV=y
+CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_ALTBOOTCMD=y
 CONFIG_OF_SYSTEM_SETUP=y
 CONFIG_DEFAULT_FDT_FILE="mediatek/mt7986a-bpi-r3-mini.dtb"
 CONFIG_LOGLEVEL=7
